---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Orks Beginner's Guide - Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Orks? Learn the lore, how the WAAAGH! works on the table, how to paint a green horde fast, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">💀</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Orks</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Green. Loud. Absolutely not interested in your opinion. Orks are a fungal alien species
            that reproduces via spores, builds technology that shouldn't work, and genuinely
            just loves to fight. They're the most fun faction in the game. We said what we said.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Melee Horde</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy ✓</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160-$220</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Orks?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Orks are not animals. They're fungal organisms - closer to a mushroom than a mammal.
          They reproduce by releasing spores when they die, meaning an Ork invasion of a planet
          is effectively permanent. Kill every Ork and the planet still has Orks in fifty years
          when the spores germinate. There is no winning. There is only containing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their technology is the best joke in the setting. An Ork's rocket pack shouldn't fly.
          Their guns shouldn't shoot that far. Their vehicles shouldn't run at all.
          But they do - because Orks collectively believe they will.
          There's a low-level psychic field generated by Ork minds that literally warps reality
          to match their expectations. Paint a vehicle red and it goes faster.
          Because every Ork knows red wunz go fasta.
        </p>
        <p>
          The more Orks gather, the more powerful this field becomes. A WAAAGH! -
          a great migration of Orks drawn together by psychic energy and shared love of violence -
          can grow to a size that threatens entire star systems.
          History's largest WAAAGH! brought together trillions of Orks.
          The Imperium has never fully recovered from it.
        </p>
        <p>
          They have a caste system of sorts: Boyz are the core warriors. Nobz are the bigger,
          meaner veterans. Warbosses lead through violence (the biggest Ork is always in charge).
          Mekboyz build the vehicles. Painboyz perform surgery. Gretchin are the tiny,
          cowardly goblins who do all the work nobody else wants to do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Orks are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">melee horde</strong>. The goal is simple:
          get across the table as fast as possible and hit things very hard with very large weapons.
          You'll have more models than your opponent. Probably a lot more.
        </p>
        <p>
          Individual Orks are surprisingly resilient — they have multiple wounds each,
          meaning it takes several hits to bring one down rather than a single lucky shot.
          But they die in numbers, and that's fine. You have numbers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ork shooting is deliberately bad. They hit on 5s with most units -
          out of six possible results on a die, they need a 5 or 6 to hit anything.
          This is lore-accurate (they point in the general direction and pull the trigger)
          and means the army isn't meant to win through firepower.
          You advance, you survive the incoming fire, and then you charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          The community shorthand is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">"Get Green Done"</strong> -
          paint fast, field a lot, have fun. It's the most relaxed faction culture in the hobby.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Orks are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want to get in close and hit things very hard</li>
            <li>✓ You love the idea of a chaotic, unpredictable army</li>
            <li>✓ You want a fast, forgiving paint scheme</li>
            <li>✓ You want the faction with the best personality</li>
            <li>✓ You want quantity over quality - lots of models on the table</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want to win through precision shooting</li>
            <li>✗ You don't want to assemble and paint 40+ models</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer elegant, disciplined armies</li>
            <li>✗ You want powerful psychic abilities</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Orks</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">
        Here's the secret: messy is correct. Battle-damaged, grimy, and rough IS the Ork aesthetic.
        You cannot fail.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        The main thing you're painting is green skin, brown leather, and dirty metal.
        All three of those benefit from washes and drybrushing - the two techniques that hide mistakes automatically.
        Orks are genuinely one of the best factions to learn to paint on.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Grey Seer (or Wraithbone)</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A light neutral base coat works better than black for Orks - the green skin pops more, and the leather browns read cleaner.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Ork Flesh Contrast paint over all skin</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Slap it on every green area. It self-shades, creates depth in the muscles, and looks great in one coat. This is the fastest method and it works.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wyldwood Contrast on leather and cloth</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Straps, belts, loincloths, boots - one coat of Wyldwood gives you instant dark brown leather that already looks worn and dirty. Perfect.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leadbelcher on all metal</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Weapons, armor plates, choppas, shootas - drybrush or dab Leadbelcher over anything metallic. Don't be neat. Orks aren't neat.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Agrax Earthshade wash over everything</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A brown-black wash over the whole model. It ties all the colors together, adds grime and shadow, and makes everything look like it's been dragged through a warzone. Which it has.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush Warboss Green on skin, Ironbreaker on metal</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Bring raised surfaces back to life. The drybrush makes muscles pop on the skin and adds scratches and wear to the metal for free.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">7</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Ushabti Bone on teeth and tusks, base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">One detail that elevates the whole model. Pick out the teeth and tusk tips. Then base with a brown texture paint and a tuft.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The "Get Green Done" philosophy</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Ork players have a saying: "A painted Ork is better than an unpainted Ork."
          The community actively celebrates speed painting, batch painting, and
          "good enough for the table." You are not expected to spend 10 hours per model.
          You have 60 of them. Paint them in batches of 10, keep moving, and enjoy the chaos.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">One box to start. Paint it before you buy more - trust the process.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Orks</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Beastboss (your warlord), 20 Beast Snagga Boyz (your core troops — tougher 
          than standard Boyz and born to hunt monsters), and 4 Squighog Boyz with a Bomb Squig 
          (elite cavalry on giant squigs). A hard-hitting Beast Snagga themed force out of the box.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D14VVJ26?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Ork Boyz (20-model box)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Boyz means more chaos. The second purchase for almost every new Ork player.
          Boyz are cheap in points, easy to paint in batches, and flooding the board with them
          is one of the most fun experiences in 40k. You will want more.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=beast+snagga+boyz+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Grey Seer Spray', use: 'Base coat - neutral primer for contrast paints', required: true },
            { name: 'Ork Flesh (Contrast)', use: 'Skin - one coat, self-shading', required: true },
            { name: 'Wyldwood (Contrast)', use: 'Leather straps, cloth, and belts', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Metal weapons and armor', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Full model wash - grime and shadow', required: true },
            { name: 'Warboss Green', use: 'Drybrush highlight on skin', required: true },
            { name: 'Ironbreaker', use: 'Drybrush highlight on metal', required: false },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone', use: 'Teeth, tusks, and bone details', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> - {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$42 for the full set. You'll use every one of these on every model.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Orks', cost: '~$160', note: 'Beastboss, Beast Snagga Boyz, Squighog Boyz' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$42', note: 'Contrast paints + wash + drybush colors' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Brown texture paint + tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Some Ork models are multi-part resin/plastic' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$239</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Orks are a horde army - budget for more Boyz eventually.
        The Combat Patrol gets you started, but you'll want 40-60 Boyz for a full competitive list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">WAAAGH!</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Grab the Combat Patrol. Paint ten Boyz before you do anything else.
        Then paint ten more. Then never stop painting Orks. This is the way.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
